{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/875404-question-on-thread-necromancy","id":875404,"title":"Question on thread necromancy??","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-27T00:44:35-07:00","id":875404,"title":"Question on thread necromancy??","content":"Though i see nothing in the forum rules (as linked when i got here), is there any sort of 'unwritten rule' on how far back someone can go into an old thread to 'bring it back up? Some sites i go to, consider it bad form (unless you are the threat originator) to go back more than 2-3 months, while other site actually encourage people to go back to the 'beginning' to bring up old threads as long as you have something substantive to offer and there's even one forum i go to, that hits you with a 'warning' if you bring up threads older than a year, wanting you to make up a NEW one for the same topic....<br /> <br /> As mentioned to someone already in 'pms', i have gone back 2 of the 6 pages worth in the main classic WoD area, and have just finished the first of 10 pages of old stuff in the werewolf area..<br /> So before i got too far back in the older threads, i figured i would ask for a heads up before continuing..<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T00:55:58-07:00","id":875411,"title":"","content":"Generally frowned upon, largely because if everyone thought there were still points to be made they'd still be posting in those threads.<br /> <br /> This belongs in Off-Topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T06:41:11-07:00","id":875567,"title":"","content":"There's no rule against it, and we don't infract people for it, but the practice is generally seen as bad form by the member base from what I can tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T06:50:21-07:00","id":875574,"title":"","content":"Yeah it's more of a general netiquette thing than any specific rule we have. I'd say if you're going back more than a couple of months, you're probably better starting anew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T07:20:41-07:00","id":875606,"title":"","content":"Occasionally a topic will come up where you have a new experience or new wrinkle that is relevant to an old thread. But even then, it's probably smarter to just post a link to the old thread than to necro it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T12:00:09-07:00","id":875821,"title":"","content":"So i am close to (if not already over) my unwritten limit of what i can go back and 'resurrect'.. Got it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T01:54:33-07:00","id":879389,"title":"","content":"I usually will just start a new thread if the other has been dead tok long. But sometimes, the point directly relates to something said in the previous thread and almost need it to be fulky relevant. So then I'll bring it back so the full discussion is available.<br /> <br /> Edit: or art threads. Themed art threads, like the Inspiration trhead in the Exalted forum, should be necromancied for new additions just to keep it in one place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","user":"vampire hunter D","date":". 05-01-2016, 05:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T12:19:41-07:00","id":879617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/875404-question-on-thread-necromancy?p=875821#post875821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So i am close to (if not already over) my unwritten limit of what i can go back and 'resurrect'.. Got it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say that. I at least, and I'd assume at least a few others, see the spate of necros as one incident of a relatively new poster learning the norms of this forum. Starting this thread also helps because it shows you're not going to make it a pattern going forward, and any necros you do choose to do are going to be more considered.<br /> <br /> Also to add to vampire hunter D's post, threads like, &quot;my favorite/hated X&quot; are also good ones for necroing without rubbing people the wrong way. They tend to be light on deep discussions (so people don't feel like your reopening something that was beaten to death already), and they're good ways to say a bit about your tastes/game-style to the forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}